#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# multivariate_poisson_distribution

#% text
# `multivariate_poisson_distribution(m0, [m1, ..., mk])` is the distribution of the vector `[Y0 + Y1, ..., Y0 + Yk]` of sums of independent Poisson variables `Y0` of mean `m0` and `Yi` of mean `mi`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The mean is `[m0 + m1, ..., m0 + mk]`; the covariance matrix has `m0 + mi` on the diagonal and `m0` elsewhere.

#% item
# `pdf(d, [x1, ..., xk])` sums over the common part `j` from 0 to the least `xi`.

#% item
# `random_variate(d)` and `random_variate(d, n)` draw one or `n` vectors.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mean(multivariate_poisson_distribution(1, [2, 3]))
#% output
#= [3, 4]

#% cell
covariance(multivariate_poisson_distribution(1, [2, 3]))
#% output
#= [[3, 1], [1, 4]]

#% cell
pdf(multivariate_poisson_distribution(1, [2, 3]), [1, 1])
#% output
#= 7/exp(6)

#% cell
length(random_variate(multivariate_poisson_distribution(1, [2, 3]), 5))
#% output
#= 5

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `poisson_distribution`, `wishart_matrix_distribution`, `covariance`
